codex
There’s a better accounting issue: setup-path sample counts subtract Cholesky/solve FLOPs even though those FLOPs happen in setup, outside the per-MLP budget. I’m separating setup sample counts from fallback sample counts so precomputed MLPs can use more rows without increasing predict FLOPs.
